## Failures

### AC2b — missing `tenant_id` filter (FAIL)

- Expected (refined ticket Requirements §1 and user prompt AC2 bullet 2):
  `.eq('tenant_id', tenantId).eq('student_id', studentId)`
- Actual (`app/teacher/start-teaching/students/[studentId]/page.tsx:165–170`):
  ```ts
  const { data, error } = await sb
    .from('lesson_completions')
    .select('completed_at, notes, module_id')
    .eq('student_id', studentId)
    .order('completed_at', { ascending: false })
    .limit(1);
  ```
- Why this matters: the LR-13c canonical pattern at
  `app/teacher/curriculum/[chapter]/[group]/[module]/page.tsx:240–247`
  filters by both `tenant_id` and `student_id`. RLS on
  `lesson_completions` (fresh-setup.sql:377–378) protects against
  cross-tenant reads at runtime, so this is not a security bug,
  but it is an explicit AC violation: defense-in-depth and pattern
  consistency are missing.
- Bug filed:
  `docs/features/launch-readiness/iterations/lr-13d-latest-observation-callout-on-student-profile/bugs/kan-149-lr-13d-missing-tenant-id-filter-bug-latest-observation.md`
- Severity: P2 (correctness/consistency, not security at runtime
  thanks to RLS).

## Notes

- AC2e (try/catch for 42703) — the item the prompt called out as
  HARD required — is correctly implemented. Code path:
  - On any thrown error, the catch block reads `pgCode` from
    `(err as { code?: string }).code`.
  - If `pgCode === '42703'`, the error is silently swallowed (no
    console.error).
  - Otherwise, the error is logged with a `'LR-13d load
    latestObservation:'` prefix.
  - Either way, `setLatestObservation(null)` is called → no callout
    renders (guarded by `latestObservation && latestObservation.notes?.trim()`).
- The only blocker on a PASS is the missing `tenant_id` filter on
  the query.
